The fixed lapse source and kappa damping terms are lower order and do not
increase the frozen-coefficient principal-speed envelope. Using the requested
coordinate-speed convention v_+ = -beta_x+c and v_- = -beta_x-c gives:

sector c
physical 1
constraint_Z4 1
lapse sqrt(2)=1.414213562373
shift_transverse sqrt(0.75)=0.866025403784
shift_longitudinal_d4 sqrt(0.75*(2-2/4))=1.060660171780

Thus c_max=sqrt(2), from the lapse sector. This is a conservative local
frozen-coefficient envelope, not a complete characteristic diagonalization
of the reduced live system. In particular, no complete principal-system
proof is claimed.

