CLASSIFICATION
EXCISION_PLACEMENT_NOT_SUFFICIENT

The old placement is not strictly outside the conservative fastest envelope,
but moving the face inward to x=0.375 does not cure the instability. Both
provisional-boundary resolutions become inadmissible before t=8, the fine
run fails earlier, constraints and radial Nyquist content explode, and the
optional exact-GP control fails still earlier. D9 therefore does not confirm
excision placement as the cause. Perturbations and the k scan remain
suspended.
